			{/* ===== Section 09: Circuits ===== */}
			<section id="circuits" class="mb-24 scroll-mt-20">
				<div class="mb-8 flex items-baseline gap-4">
					<span class="font-mono text-sm text-accent/60">09</span>
					<div>
						<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-accent-2 sm:text-3xl">Circuits</h2>
						<p class="mt-1 text-base text-textColor/60">Cross-layer head composition and mechanistic interpretability</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				{/* Linkage callout */}
				<div class="linkage-callout reveal linkage-circuits">
					<span class="linkage-icon">&uarr;</span>
					<span>
						Individual attention heads learn single relational patterns (§04&ndash;05).
						This section examines how heads across <strong>different layers</strong>
						compose via the residual stream to implement multi-step algorithms.
					</span>
				</div>

				<div class="section-prose reveal">
					<p>
						Because the residual stream is a shared linear workspace, a head in layer <code>L+1</code>
						can read the output of a head in layer <code>L</code> &mdash; the two compose via matrix
						multiplication through the residual stream. When specific heads across layers cooperate
						to implement a coherent function, the result is a <strong>circuit</strong>: a multi-step
						algorithm distributed across the network’s computational
						graph.<span class="sn-marker" data-sn="sn-circuits-olah">28</span>
					</p>
				</div>

				{/* Induction Head Circuit Diagram */}
				<div class="circ-induction-wrap reveal">
					<div class="circ-induction-title">The induction head circuit</div>
					<div class="circ-induction-subtitle">Two heads across two layers learn to copy patterns</div>

					{/* Token sequence */}
					<div class="circ-sequence">
						<div class="circ-seq-label">Input sequence:</div>
						<div class="circ-tokens">
							<span class="circ-tok">&hellip;</span>
							<span class="circ-tok circ-tok-a">A</span>
							<span class="circ-tok circ-tok-b">B</span>
							<span class="circ-tok">&hellip;</span>
							<span class="circ-tok circ-tok-a">A</span>
							<span class="circ-tok circ-tok-predict">?</span>
						</div>
					</div>

					{/* Two-layer circuit diagram */}
					<div class="circ-layers">
						{/* Layer 1: Previous-Token Head */}
						<div class="circ-layer">
							<div class="circ-layer-label">Layer <em>L</em></div>
							<div class="circ-head-card circ-head-prev">
