						</div>

						{/* Layer 2: Induction Head */}
						<div class="circ-layer">
							<div class="circ-layer-label">Layer <em>L+1</em></div>
							<div class="circ-head-card circ-head-induction">
								<div class="circ-head-name">Induction Head</div>
								<div class="circ-head-desc">
									The second A attends to <strong>B</strong> (the token that followed A last time).
									It reads: &ldquo;After A came B before, so B should come next.&rdquo;
								</div>
								{/* Mini heatmap */}
								<div class="circ-mini-heatmap">
									<div class="circ-hm-header">
										<span class="circ-hm-corner">Q&darr; K&rarr;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-col">&hellip;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-col circ-hm-col-a">A</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-col circ-hm-col-b">B</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-col">&hellip;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-col circ-hm-col-a">A</span>
									</div>
									<div class="circ-hm-row">
										<span class="circ-hm-row-label">&hellip;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
									</div>
									<div class="circ-hm-row">
										<span class="circ-hm-row-label circ-hm-col-a">A</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
									</div>
									<div class="circ-hm-row">
										<span class="circ-hm-row-label circ-hm-col-b">B</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
									</div>
									<div class="circ-hm-row">
										<span class="circ-hm-row-label">&hellip;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.3">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
									</div>
									<div class="circ-hm-row">
										<span class="circ-hm-row-label circ-hm-col-a">A<sub>2</sub></span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.1">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.1">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell circ-hm-hot circ-hm-induction" style="opacity:0.95">0.89</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.1">&middot;</span>
										<span class="circ-hm-cell" style="opacity:0.15">&middot;</span>
									</div>
								</div>
								<div class="circ-head-insight">The second A attends to B &mdash; predicting &ldquo;B comes next&rdquo;</div>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					{/* Circuit result */}
					<div class="circ-result">
						<div class="circ-result-arrow">&darr;</div>
						<div class="circ-result-box">
							<strong>Result:</strong> The model predicts <strong class="circ-tok-b-text">B</strong>
							after the second <strong class="circ-tok-a-text">A</strong> &mdash;
							it learned to copy patterns from context.
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="section-prose reveal">
					<p>
						This <strong>induction head</strong> circuit was characterized by Olsson et al.
						(2022)<span class="sn-marker" data-sn="sn-induction">29</span> and explains a
						significant fraction of in-context learning: the ability to continue patterns from
						few-shot examples. The previous-token head (layer <code>L</code>) writes
						&ldquo;the token before me&rdquo; into B’s residual stream; the induction head
						(layer <code>L+1</code>) uses this to match [A] &rarr; [B] and predict B after the
						second A. Other documented circuits include:
					</p>
				</div>

				{/* Circuit types gallery */}
				<div class="circ-types reveal">
					<div class="circ-type-card">
						<div class="circ-type-name">Induction Heads</div>
						<div class="circ-type-desc">Copy patterns: &ldquo;[A][B]&hellip;[A] &rarr; predict [B]&rdquo;</div>
						<div class="circ-type-tag">In-context learning</div>
					</div>
					<div class="circ-type-card">
						<div class="circ-type-name">Duplicate Token Heads</div>
						<div class="circ-type-desc">Detect when a token has appeared before in the sequence</div>
						<div class="circ-type-tag">Copy suppression</div>
					</div>
					<div class="circ-type-card">
						<div class="circ-type-name">Name Mover Heads</div>
						<div class="circ-type-desc">Move a name from its first mention to where it&rsquo;s needed later</div>
						<div class="circ-type-tag">Indirect object identification</div>
					</div>
					<div class="circ-type-card">
						<div class="circ-type-name">Backup Heads</div>
						<div class="circ-type-desc">Compensate when primary heads are ablated &mdash; redundancy in the network</div>
						<div class="circ-type-tag">Robustness</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="section-prose reveal">
					<p>
						Identifying these circuits is the core methodology of <strong>mechanistic
						interpretability</strong><span class="sn-marker" data-sn="sn-mi-olah">30</span> &mdash;
						reverse-engineering the algorithms implemented by trained neural networks at the
						resolution of individual components, rather than treating the model as a black box.
					</p>
				</div>

				{/* Why mechanistic interpretability matters */}
				<div class="mi-teaser reveal">
					<div class="mi-teaser-label">Why it matters</div>
					<div class="mi-teaser-cards">
						<div class="mi-teaser-card mi-card-safety">
							<div class="mi-card-icon">&Delta;</div>
							<div class="mi-card-title">Safety</div>
							<div class="mi-card-desc">If we can identify the circuits behind model behavior, we can catch failure modes <em>before</em> deployment &mdash; not after.</div>
						</div>
						<div class="mi-teaser-card mi-card-understanding">
							<div class="mi-card-icon">&oplus;</div>
							<div class="mi-card-title">Understanding</div>
							<div class="mi-card-desc">Moving beyond &ldquo;it works&rdquo; to <em>how</em> it works. Circuits give us a scientific vocabulary for transformer computation.</div>
						</div>
						<div class="mi-teaser-card mi-card-control">
							<div class="mi-card-icon">&sect;</div>
							<div class="mi-card-title">Control</div>
							<div class="mi-card-desc">Once you know which heads implement a behavior, you can steer, edit, or ablate it &mdash; precise intervention instead of blunt fine-tuning.</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="section-prose reveal">
					<p>
						The transformer architecture admits principled scientific investigation:
						its linear residual stream, discrete attention patterns, and structured layer
						composition make it more amenable to reverse-engineering than arbitrary neural
						networks. Recent work on sparse autoencoders and dictionary
						learning<span class="sn-marker" data-sn="sn-saes">31</span> has begun decomposing
						residual stream representations into interpretable features.
					</p>
				</div>

				{/* Closing: tying back to the preamble */}
				<div class="circ-closing reveal">
					<div class="circ-closing-divider"></div>
					<div class="circ-closing-journey">
						<div class="circ-closing-title">The journey</div>
						<div class="circ-journey-steps">
							<span class="circ-j-step circ-j-embed">Tokens</span>
							<span class="circ-j-arrow">&rarr;</span>
							<span class="circ-j-step circ-j-embed">Embeddings</span>
							<span class="circ-j-arrow">&rarr;</span>
							<span class="circ-j-step circ-j-attn">Attention</span>
							<span class="circ-j-arrow">&rarr;</span>
							<span class="circ-j-step circ-j-ffn">FFN</span>
							<span class="circ-j-arrow">&rarr;</span>
							<span class="circ-j-step circ-j-output">Prediction</span>
							<span class="circ-j-arrow">&rarr;</span>
							<span class="circ-j-step circ-j-circuits">Circuits</span>
						</div>
					</div>

					{/* Opened box — mirrors the preamble\'s closed black box */}
					<div class="mi-openbox-wrap reveal">
						<div class="mi-openbox-label-in">tokens in</div>
						<div class="mi-openbox">
							<span class="mi-ob-component mi-ob-embed" title="Embedding">E</span>
							<span class="mi-ob-arrow">&rarr;</span>
							<span class="mi-ob-component mi-ob-attn" title="Attention">A</span>
							<span class="mi-ob-arrow">&rarr;</span>
							<span class="mi-ob-component mi-ob-ffn" title="FFN">F</span>
							<span class="mi-ob-arrow">&rarr;</span>
							<span class="mi-ob-component mi-ob-output" title="Prediction">P</span>
						</div>
						<div class="mi-openbox-label-out">prediction out</div>
					</div>

					<p class="circ-closing-text">
						The transformer’s forward pass is fully characterized: tokenization, embedding,
						positional encoding, self-attention, FFN, residual connections, layer normalization,
						unembedding, and softmax. The circuits framework connects these low-level operations
						to high-level algorithmic behaviors, opening a path toward mechanistic understanding
						of learned computation.
					</p>

					{/* Follow-up post callout */}
