			// BUT the conceptual meaning changes: rows are now d_head dimensions, columns are tokens
			// We transpose the actual values: kValues[r][c] -> transposed[c][r] ... but we only show 3 rows
			// K is 3 displayed rows x 8 cols, K^T should look different: fewer columns (d_head=3+dots), more rows (T=8)
			// Actually: K = (T x d_head) = 8 rows x 3 cols but we show it as 3 displayed rows x 8 cols
			// K^T = (d_head x T) = 3 rows x 8 cols — same visual grid size!
			// The key visual: token labels move from being column headers to column headers still,
